iterations.reply:
I wrote the node with only the granted `response-channel` import. I left out both of operations' requests, because the node's `with` clause grants no filesystem or network interface:

- **Log file:** appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` would need a filesystem capability.
- **Metadata fetch:** calling `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich` would need `http-client`.

Adding either would need the graph's `with` clause to change. Sending the input's text to an outside service would also be worth a separate review.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::response_channel;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        let c = response_channel::send(&reply.text);
        DeliveryConfirmation {
            session: c.session,
            delivered: c.delivered,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

